WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.180
Has anyone ever told you that you need  to have a clear goal

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.200
in order to achieve something or get better.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:11.800
According to modern learning science the opposite is true

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.180
for example

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:19.560
the best surfers are not those that train to win a prize or to be featured  in a glossy magazine,

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.000
but those that play with the waves everyday,  because they love it.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.960
This technique argues that you get 
better  at something

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.120
focus  on the process of learning

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.320
and not the outcome a 
product too far away to motivate you.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.600
In a Stanford University design experiment,

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.200
a pottery teacher split the class into two groups

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.100
the first group focused  on making as many clay pots as they wanted

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:52.440
the second  on making one single very 
beautiful pot.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.860
At the end that teacher graded the pots and announce the winner,

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.100
the results were clear

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.100
all the best pots 
came from students that made many pots

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.420
not those that tried making one single 
winning piece of art.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.660
To optimize process learning,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.700
set a fixed study time  
in which you focus on the material for say

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:16.660
25 minutes a day

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.299
in that time

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:22.340
don't try to reach a certain goal like 
reading an entire chapter

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:25.960
just learn for the exact amount of time that you set yourself

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.960
then stop.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.260
Process learning will help you feel more relaxed 
during your study

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:35.100
and give you a sense of accomplishment once you are done.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.460
the very affect that you were interrupted

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.580
in the middle of your practice before 
reaching a milestone,

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:41.790
keeps interest up

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:45.410
and increases the motivation to continue 
the next day.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.160
